            <ArticleTitle>Phenytoin (Epanutin) Associated Hodgkin's Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of phenytoin-associated Hodgkin's disease of lymphocyte predominance subtype, which developed after two years of phenytoin (Epanutin) treatment. Four other English cases of phenytoin-associated lmphoid malignancy are also reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
